        "content": "Excellent! Now I have comprehensive information. Let me create a summary document with the house style patterns found:\n\n## House Style Patterns Found in .NET Release Notes\n\nBased on my analysis of existing preview release notes in the repository (specifically `.NET 10 Preview 3`, `Preview 4`, and `.NET 9 Preview 3`), here are the established conventions:\n\n### **1. PR Link Format**\n**Pattern:** `[dotnet/REPOSITORY #NNNNN](URL)`\n- **WITH space** between repository name and hash (e.g., `dotnet/runtime #108913`)\n- Links point to either `/pull/NNNNN` or `/issues/NNNNN` on GitHub\n- **Examples:**\n  - `[dotnet/runtime #108913](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/issues/108913)`\n  - `[dotnet/runtime #114191](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/114191)`\n  - `[dotnet/runtime #102704](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/102704)`\n\n**Files showing pattern:**\n- `/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/10.0/preview/preview3/runtime.md` (lines 91, 101)\n- `/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/10.0/preview/preview4/runtime.md` (lines 48, 74-77)\n\n---\n\n### **2. Section Heading Format**\n**Pattern:** Double hash `##` for main section headings (H2)\n\n**Structure:**\n```markdown\n## Section Title with Title Case\n```\n\n**Examples from runtime.md:**\n- `## Stack Allocation of Small Arrays of Reference Types`\n- `## Improved Code Layout`\n- `## Escape Analysis for Local Struct Fields`\n- `## Inlining Improvements`\n\n**Files:**\n- `/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/10.0/preview/preview3/runtime.md` (lines 12, 93)\n- `/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/10.0/preview/preview4/runtime.md` (lines 12, 70)\n\n---\n\n### **3. Component-Level File Structure**\n**Typical markdown files:** `runtime.md`, `libraries.md`, `aspnetcore.md`, `sdk.md`, `csharp.md`, `efcore.md`, etc.\n\n**Standard structure:**\n```markdown\n# Component Name in .NET Version Preview X - Release Notes\n\nHere's a summary of what's new in [Component] in this preview release:\n\n- [Section Title](#anchor)\n- [Another Section](#anchor2)\n\nComponent updates in .NET Version:\n\n- [What's new in .NET X](docs_link) documentation\n- [Breaking changes](docs_link) (if applicable)\n- [Roadmap](github_link) (if applicable)\n\n## Section Title\n\n[Content describing the feature]\n\n## Another Section\n\n[Content describing another feature]\n```\n\n**File examples:**\n- `/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/10.0/preview/preview3/runtime.md`\n- `/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/10.0/preview/preview3/libraries.md`\n- `/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/10.0/preview/preview3/aspnetcore.md`\n\n---\n\n### **4. Table of Contents Pattern**\n**Format:** Each major section is listed as a bullet point with a markdown anchor link\n```markdown\n- [Section Title](#section-title-in-lowercase-with-hyphens)\n- [Another Title](#another-title-in-lowercase-with-hyphens)\n```\n\n**Example from aspnetcore.md (lines 5-13):**\n```markdown\n- [Declarative model for persisting state from components and services](#declarative-model-for-persisting-state-from-components-and-services)\n- [Reference fingerprinted static web assets in standalone Blazor WebAssembly apps](#reference-fingerprinted-static-web-assets-in-standalone-blazor-webassembly-apps)\n```\n\n---\n\n### **5. Header Structure Hierarchy**\n- **H1 (`#`):** Document title (e.g., \"# .NET Runtime in .NET 10 Preview 3 - Release Notes\")\n- **H2 (`##`):** Section headings for features\n- **No H3+ headings** in the component-level markdown files observed\n\n---\n\n### **6. Feature Documentation Pattern**\nEach feature section typically includes:\n1. Brief introductory sentence(s)\n2. Context/motivation (if applicable)\n3. Code examples (in markdown code blocks with language specified)\n4. Assembly/IL code samples (when performance-related)\n5. Linked PR reference (with `[dotnet/repo #NNNNN](url)` format)\n6. Before/after comparisons (for improvements)",
