    "output": "1. # Libraries Examples\n2. \n3. ## Post-Quantum Cryptography Updates\n4. \n5. ### ML-DSA\n6. \n7. The `System.Security.Cryptography.MLDsa` class gained ease-of-use updates in this release, allowing some common code patterns to be simplified:\n8. \n9. ```diff\n10. private static byte[] SignData(string privateKeyPath, ReadOnlySpan<byte> data)\n11. {\n12.     using (MLDsa signingKey = MLDsa.ImportFromPem(File.ReadAllBytes(privateKeyPath)))\n13.     {\n14. -       byte[] signature = new byte[signingKey.Algorithm.SignatureSizeInBytes];\n15. -       signingKey.SignData(data, signature);\n16. +       return signingKey.SignData(data);\n17. -       return signature;\n18.     }\n19. }\n20. ```\n21. \n22. Additionally, this release added support for HashML-DSA, which we call \"PreHash\" to help distinguish it from \"pure\" ML-DSA. As the underlying specification interacts with the Object Identifier (OID) value, the SignPreHash and VerifyPreHash methods on this `[Experimental]` type take the dotted-decimal OID as a string. This may evolve as more scenarios using HashML-DSA become well-defined.\n23. \n24. ```csharp\n25. private static byte[] SignPreHashSha3_256(MLDsa signingKey, ReadOnlySpan<byte> data)\n26. {\n27.     const string Sha3_256Oid = \"2.16.840.1.101.3.4.2.8\";\n28.     return signingKey.SignPreHash(SHA3_256.HashData(data), Sha3_256Oid);\n29. }\n30. ```\n31. \n32. ### Composite ML-DSA\n33. \n34. This release also introduces new types to support ietf-lamps-pq-composite-sigs (currently at draft 7), and an implementation of the primitive methods for RSA variants.\n35. \n36. ```csharp\n37. var algorithm = CompositeMLDsaAlgorithm.MLDsa65WithRSA4096Pss;\n38. using var privateKey = CompositeMLDsa.GenerateKey(algorithm);\n39. \n40. byte[] data = [42];\n41. byte[] signature = privateKey.SignData(data);\n42. \n43. using var publicKey = CompositeMLDsa.ImportCompositeMLDsaPublicKey(\n44.     algorithm, privateKey.ExportCompositeMLDsaPublicKey());\n45. Console.WriteLine(publicKey.VerifyData(data, signature)); // True\n46. \n47. signature[0] ^= 1; // Tamper with signature\n48. Console.WriteLine(publicKey.VerifyData(data, signature)); // False\n49. ```\n50. \n51. ---\n52. Source: [.NET 10 Preview 7 — Libraries](../../../../../release-notes/10.0/preview/preview7/libraries.md)\n53. Commentary: Long — subheadings organize related-but-distinct features. Uses `diff` blocks for API simplification and complete runnable scenarios for new APIs.\n54. Why it works: The `diff` block immediately shows the simplification (red lines removed, green line added). The Composite ML-DSA sample is a complete scenario (generate → sign → verify → tamper → verify-fails).\n55. Style note: L7 \"gained ease-of-use updates\" is passive and vague. Prefer active/direct: \"Common patterns using `MLDsa` are now easier:\" or \"Ease-of-use updates simplify common `MLDsa` patterns:\".\n56. \n57. ---\n58. "
