    "output": "## Editorial Review: .NET 11 Preview 3 Draft Release Notes\n\n### Issues Found\n\n| # | File | Heading | Issue | Suggested Rewrite |\n|---|------|---------|-------|-------------------|\n| 1 | runtime.md | `Runtime Async (V3)` | Parenthetical version is non-standard; heading doesn't use action verb or noun-first per rubric. | `## Runtime async: AOT compilation and lower allocation cost` |\n| 2 | runtime.md | *(intro paragraph)* | \"delivers two significant…advances\" is promotional. \"introduced in Preview 1 and refined in Preview 2\" is passive recap, not actionable. Cut or replace. | Delete the paragraph. The subheadings already orient the reader. |\n| 3 | runtime.md | `crossgen2 support` | 2-word heading (below 3-word minimum). \"crossgen2\" is unexplained jargon—most .NET developers don't know the AOT tool by internal name. | `### Ahead-of-time compilation for async methods` |\n| 4 | runtime.md | `Continuation reuse` | 2-word heading (below 3-word minimum). | `### Reuse continuations to cut GC pressure` |\n| 5 | runtime.md | `Profiler and diagnostic tool support` | `GetNativeCodeInfo` dropped without context. No WHY for the general reader—who was affected, what broke? Score: 4. | Add: \"Previously, profilers misattributed time spent in runtime-async methods because thunk frames were invisible to `GetNativeCodeInfo`.\" |\n| 6 | runtime.md | `GC regions on macOS` | \"Apple silicon workloads in particular may benefit from more predictable heap growth\" is speculative with no data. \"may benefit\" is weak. | Cut the Apple silicon sentence. End with: \"This brings macOS to parity with Windows and Linux, which have used regions since .NET 8.\" |\n| 7 | runtime.md | `SDSU interval register allocation` | Opaque jargon heading. Score: 2 (mystery) for ≥80 % of readers. Violates 80/20 filter. No observable user outcome stated. | Demote to a bullet under a new `### JIT code-quality improvements` roll-up: \"The JIT now keeps short-lived values in registers across helper calls, reducing spills and shrinking generated code.\" |\n| 8 | libraries.md | *(title)* | Title has `- Release Notes` suffix absent from runtime.md and aspnetcore.md. Inconsistent cross-file. | Use `# .NET Libraries in .NET 11 Preview 3` (no suffix) for consistency. |\n| 9 | libraries.md | `SafeFileHandle.CreateAnonymousPipe` | Opens in API-inventory mode (\"A new static factory method creates…\"). WHY comes three paragraphs later. Lead with the problem. | \"Creating anonymous pipes with independent async control on each end previously required P/Invoke or platform-specific code. `SafeFileHandle.CreateAnonymousPipe` eliminates that:\" |\n| 10 | libraries.md | `FileStream async handles on Unix` / `RandomAccess on non-seekable files` | Both are nested under the `SafeFileHandle.CreateAnonymousPipe` heading but are independent features. Misleading hierarchy. | Promote each to a peer `##` section, or group all three under a new `## File I/O improvements` parent. |\n| 11 | libraries.md | `HashSet<T> and Dictionary<T> improvements` | **`Dictionary<T>` is not a real type**—the correct name is `Dictionary<TKey, TValue>`. Violates \"no invented API names.\" Heading also uses vague \"improvements\" with no concrete delta or benchmark number. | Heading: `### Faster HashSet and Dictionary lookups`. Body: fix to `Dictionary<TKey, TValue>` and add a benchmark percentage if available. |\n| 12 | libraries.md | `Community contributors` | Empty placeholder—no contributor list. Either populate or remove. | List contributors or delete the section. |\n| 13 | aspnetcore.md | `Virtualize component supports variable-height items` | Prose says \"supply an `ItemSize` callback instead of a fixed `ItemSize` value\" but the code example shows **neither**—no `ItemSize` callback appears. Readers who copy-paste will not get the new behavior. | Add the `ItemSize` callback to the code sample, or if the new behavior is automatic (no `ItemSize` needed), rewrite the prose to say \"omit `ItemSize`; the component measures each item at render time.\" |\n| 14 | aspnetcore.md | `Azure SQL with Managed Identity in Individual Auth templates` | 9-word heading; exceeds 8-word maximum. | `### Managed Identity in Individual Auth templates` |\n| 15 | aspnetcore.md | `Virtualize…` (last sentence) | \"The component measures each rendered item and adjusts scroll estimates accordingly\"—mild anthropomorphism (\"measures\", \"adjusts\"). | \"Each rendered item is measured at paint time; scroll-position estimates update automatically.\" |\n| 16 | fsharp.md | *(intro)* | \"No significant F# feature changes are highlighted\" is negative and passive. Violates positive-tone rule. | \"Preview 3 focuses on F# compiler and tooling bug fixes.\" |\n| 17 | fsharp.md | Completion bug fix | \"no longer inconsistently filters out\" is a double negative—hard to parse. | \"IDE completion now shows obsolete fields and events, matching the behavior for other obsolete members.\" |\n| 18 | fsharp.md | *(structure)* | \"What's new in F#\" link appears at the bottom; in libraries.md and aspnetcore.md the equivalent link is near the top. Inconsistent. | Move the link block above `## Bug fixes`. |\n\n---\n\n### Highest-Priority Single Rewrite\n\n**libraries.md → `HashSet<T> and Dictionary<T> improvements`**\n\nThis entry has a **factual API-name error** (`Dictionary<T>` does not exist), a vague heading, and no concrete performance delta—three rubric violations in one section.\n\n**Current:**\n> ### HashSet\\<T> and Dictionary\\<T> improvements\n>\n> `HashSet<T>` lookup and insertion operations benefit from JIT bounds-check elimination, reducing instruction count in the hot path. `Dictionary<T>.Remove` has been restructured to produce better codegen for value-type keys, reducing unnecessary branch overhead. ([dotnet/runtime #125893](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125893), [dotnet/runtime #125884](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125884))\n\n**Rewrite:**\n> ### Faster HashSet and Dictionary operations\n>\n> `HashSet<T>` lookups and insertions now skip a redundant bounds check on the hot path, thanks to a JIT optimization that proves the index is in range. `Dictionary<TKey, TValue>.Remove` generates tighter code for value-type keys by eliminating an unnecessary branch. ([dotnet/runtime #125893](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125893), [dotnet/runtime #125884](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/pull/125884))\n\n**Why this is #1:** A wrong type name in published release notes erodes reader trust and will be quoted verbatim by bloggers and AI indexes. It is also the easiest fix—rename and tighten in one pass."
  }
]
