              "arguments": "{\"path\": \"/home/runner/work/dotnet-core-release-notes/dotnet-core-release-notes/release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/aspnetcore.md\", \"old_str\": \"### Virtualize component supports variable-height items\\n\\nThe `Virtualize` component can now render lists where items have different heights. Previously, the component required all items to share a uniform row height; that constraint is lifted in Preview 3. ([dotnet/aspnetcore #64964](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/64964))\\n\\nTo use variable-height virtualization, supply an `ItemSize` callback instead of a fixed `ItemSize` value:\\n\\n```razor\\n<Virtualize Items=\\\"items\\\" Context=\\\"item\\\">\\n    <ItemContent>\\n        <div>@item.Title</div>\\n        @if (item.HasDescription)\\n        {\\n            <p>@item.Description</p>\\n        }\\n    </ItemContent>\\n</Virtualize>\\n```\\n\\nThe component measures each rendered item and adjusts scroll estimates accordingly.\", \"new_str\": \"### Virtualize supports variable-height items\\n\\nThe `Virtualize` component now measures each item's rendered height and adjusts scroll estimates accordingly, so it works correctly with lists where items have different heights. No API change is required — existing `<Virtualize>` usage automatically benefits. ([dotnet/aspnetcore #64964](https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/pull/64964))\\n\\n```razor\\n<Virtualize Items=\\\"items\\\" Context=\\\"item\\\">\\n    <ItemContent>\\n        <div>@item.Title</div>\\n        @if (item.HasDescription)\\n        {\\n            <p>@item.Description</p>\\n        }\\n    </ItemContent>\\n</Virtualize>\\n```\\n\\n`ItemSize` is still accepted as an initial estimate for unmeasured items. Once the component measures a rendered batch, actual heights take over.\"}"
