te (fsharp `251aaf25` → `d507366c`)\n   - `fbb044efb4` (Apr 9/10) — Razor internal changes (not user-visible)\n   - `c02304eb47` (Apr 10) — F# update (`d507366c` → `1f468868`)\n   - `f5672d9470` (Apr 13) — F# update (`1f468868` → `bd2823e2`)\n\n5. **Investigated aspnetcore Azure SQL fidelity** — the previous run removed `aspnetcore#66179` (Azure SQL/Managed Identity templates) scoring it 0 as \"merged 2026-04-08 with milestone preview4\". Investigation revealed:\n   - VMR commit `a8b33e7593` (committed Apr 7, 2026) directly backported this feature to `release/11.0.1xx-preview3` branch\n   - The aspnetcore `release/11.0-preview3` branch did NOT contain it at time of previous check, but the VMR does\n   - This feature IS in preview3 (VMR is authoritative); previous run was wrong to exclude it\n   - aspnetcore#65951 (scroll stability) was correctly excluded — confirmed NOT in VMR preview3 branch\n\n6. **Investigated F# changes** — cloned fsharp repo; found 4 user-visible bug fixes in range `251aaf25` → `bd2823e2`:\n   - `#13512` — IDE completion inconsistently filtering obsolete fields/events\n   - `#5735` — Warning FS0020 wrong range in sequential expressions\n   - `#19532` — FS0452 spuriously raised for empty string in quotations\n   - `#18584` — CLIEvent not recognized as events in Symbol API\n\n7. **Made editorial changes** — updated 6 files:\n   - `changes.json` / `features.json`: Corrected Azure SQL score 0→6; added 4 new F# bug fix entries\n   - `aspnetcore.md`: Restored Azure SQL section (renamed heading to ≤8 words); fixed Virtualize section (removed incorrect ItemSize callback claim — component auto-measures, no API change needed)\n   - `fsharp.md`: Added bug fixes section; rewritten opener (positive framing); moved docs link above fixes\n   - `runtime.md`: Added title suffix; renamed headings (removed V3, renamed SDSU to plain English, renamed Profiler section, removed speculative Apple silicon claim)\n   - `libraries.md`: Restructured FileStream/RandomAccess as peers under \"File I/O improvements\" (not nested under pipes); improved all headings; removed empty Community contributors section\n\n8. **Two-model editorial review** — ran Claude Opus 4.6 and GPT-5.4 in parallel; both identified same top issues: incorrect Virtualize code sample (most critical), jargon headings in runtime.md, nesting structure in libraries.md, empty Community contributors, F# negative framing. Applied all consensus fixes.\n\n9. **Committed changes** — committed as `7cde847` with descriptive message. Renamed local branch to match remote PR branch name. Attempted to push via `push_to_pull_request_branch` safeoutputs tool — **failed** (tool not available in current tool list).\n</history>\n\n<work_done>\nFiles updated:\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/changes.json` — Corrected `aspnetcore@d1f6a83` score 0→6 with updated rationale; added 4 new F# entries (`fsharp@bd2823e`, `fsharp@5bcca43`, `fsharp@6a5df48`, `fsharp@880dda8`)\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/features.json` — Same changes as changes.json (both files have identical structure with scores)\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/aspnetcore.md` — Restored Managed Identity/Azure SQL section; fixed Virtualize description (auto-measures, no ItemSize callback API change); shortened heading to ≤8 words\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/fsharp.md` — Added Bug fixes section with 4 F# fixes; rewritten opener to lead with what's there; moved docs link above fixes section\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/runtime.md` — Added `- Release Notes` title suffix; renamed `Runtime Async (V3)` → `Runtime Async`; renamed `crossgen2 support` → `Crossgen2 support for runtime-async methods`; renamed `Profiler and diagnostic tool support` → `GetNativeCodeInfo supports async thunk methods`; removed speculative Apple silicon sentence from GC section; renamed `SDSU interval register allocation` → `Fewer register spills for single-use values`\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/libraries.md` — Restructured TOC and headings; FileStream/RandomAccess promoted to H2 under `## File I/O improvements`; renamed `WebProxy credentials from URI userinfo` → `Read proxy credentials from the URI`; renamed `HashSet<T> and Dictionary<T> improvements` → `Faster HashSet and Dictionary operations`; removed empty Community contributors section\n\nWork completed:\n- [x] Discovered active milestone (Preview 3)\n- [x] Checked VMR delta since last notes run\n- [x] Verified Azure SQL templates fidelity (confirmed it IS in preview3 via VMR direct commit)\n- [x] Investigated F# changes (4 user-visible bug fixes found)\n- [x] Updated changes.json and features.json\n- [x] Updated all markdown files\n- [x] Two-model editorial review (Claude Opus 4.6 + GPT-5.4) completed\n- [x] Applied review feedback\n- [x] Committed changes as `7cde847` on branch `release-notes/11.0-preview3-282d980949e00be5-e5cfba1ae2fcd344`\n- [ ] **Push commit to remote PR branch** — attempted but `push_to_pull_request_branch` tool not available\n- [ ] **Add daily summary comment to PR**\n- [ ] **Create PR if none exists** (needs investigation — may already exist)\n</work_done>\n\n<technical_details>\n- **VMR is authoritative**: The `dotnet/dotnet` VMR's `release/11.0.1xx-preview3` branch is the source of truth for what ships. A feature can be in preview3 even if the originating component repo (e.g., aspnetcore) has the PR tagged as preview4 — if it was directly backported to the VMR release branch.\n\n- **Azure SQL backport**: `a8b33e7593` was committed directly to VMR `release/11.0.1xx-preview3` on April 7, 2026 (before the April 9 notes run). The previous agent incorrectly excluded it by checking only the aspnetcore PR milestone date (April 8, preview4). The VMR commit is the correct reference.\n\n- **Virtualize auto-measurement**: The Blazor `Virtualize` component PR #64964 implements automatic height measurement via JavaScript after each render cycle. No `ItemSize` callback API was added — the component measures rendered items directly. The `ItemSize` parameter remains as a fallback/initial estimate. The previous draft's description of \"supply an ItemSize callback\" was factually wrong.\n\n- **Branch naming**: The workflow generates branches with `release-notes/11.0-preview3-{hash1}-{hash2}` suffixes. The local branch must be renamed to exactly match the remote branch name before pushing. Current local branch is `release-notes/11.0-preview3-282d980949e00be5-e5cfba1ae2fcd344`.\n\n- **Tool availability constraints**: `release-notes-gen` tool is not on public NuGet; requires GitHub Packages auth (GITHUB_TOKEN not available). The `push_to_pull_request_branch` safeoutputs tool was not available in the tool list at time of attempted push (tool list showed only: bash, write_bash, read_bash, stop_bash, list_bash, store_memory, view, create, edit, web_fetch, report_intent, fetch_copilot_cli_documentation, skill, sql, read_agent, list_agents, grep, glob, task).\n\n- **Network access**: git (HTTPS) works to `github.com`. `curl` is blocked. `gh` CLI is not authenticated. GitHub MCP tools listed in instructions but not directly available in tool list.\n\n- **F# commits are in preview3**: All three VMR fsharp updates (`2233e9732b`, `c02304eb47`, `f5672d9470`) happened after the April 9 00:44 UTC notes run. The F# repo was at `251aaf25da198ded` during the last run and is now at `bd2823e2d07c84f9`. All F# bug fixes in this range are new for this run.\n\n- **aspnetcore#65951 correctly excluded**: Verified that aspnetcore PR #65951 (Virtualize scroll stability) is NOT on the aspnetcore `release/11.0-preview3` branch and NOT directly committed to the VMR `release/11.0.1xx-preview3` branch. Correctly scored 0 and excluded.\n\n- **Two open questions for human review**: (1) Azure SQL backport treatment (VMR direct vs aspnetcore milestone); (2) F# bug fixes accuracy (newly added content).\n</technical_details>\n\n<important_files>\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/changes.json`\n  - Source of truth for what shipped in preview3 (21 changes + 4 new F# entries = 25 total)\n  - Added F# entries at lines ~279-340 (after aspnetcore@d1f6a83); corrected aspnetcore@d1f6a83 score at line 276\n\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/features.json`\n  - Scored version of changes.json used for editorial decisions\n  - Same structural changes as changes.json\n\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/aspnetcore.md`\n  - Blazor Virtualize and Azure SQL content\n  - Critical fix: Virtualize description now correctly says auto-measurement (not ItemSize callback)\n  - Azure SQL section restored with correct VMR PR reference\n\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/runtime.md`\n  - Runtime Async, GC, JIT content\n  - Heading renames applied throughout; speculative content removed\n\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/libraries.md`\n  - File I/O, WebProxy, HashSet/Dictionary content\n  - FileStream/RandomAccess restructured from H3-under-pipes to H2-under-File-I/O\n\n- `release-notes/11.0/preview/preview3/fsharp.md`\n  - Newly populated with 4 bug fix entries (was just a stub before)\n\n- Local git state: branch `release-notes/11.0-preview3-282d980949e00be5-e5cfba1ae2fcd344`, commit `7cde847`, 1 commit ahead of origin\n</important_files>\n\n<next_steps>\nRemaining work:\n\n1. **Push commit to remote** — need to push local commit `7cde847` to `origin/release-notes/11.0-preview3-282d980949e00be5-e5cfba1ae2fcd344`. The `push_to_pull_request_branch` safeoutputs tool should be used but was not available. Try again now that the session may have refreshed.\n\n2. **Find or create the PR** — need to check if a PR exists for `[release-notes] .NET 11 Preview 3` on `jeffhandley/dotnet-core-release-notes`. If it exists, push to it and add a comment. If not, create a draft PR.\n\n3. **Add daily summary comment to PR** — summarize: what was regenerated/updated, that VMR preview3 branch moved forward since last run (fsharp updates Apr 9-13), Azure SQL section restored (fidelity correction), F# bug fixes newly added, editorial polish from two-model review.\n\nImmediate next steps:\n- Use `push_to_pull_request_branch` safeoutput tool with branch `release-notes/11.0-preview3-282d980949e00be5-e5cfba1ae2fcd344`\n- Use `add_comment` safeoutput tool to post daily summary to the PR\n- If no PR exists, use `create_pull_request` with title `[release-notes] .NET 11 Preview 3`\n\nBlockers:\n- Need `push_to_pull_request_branch` tool to be available in current session\n- Need PR number for `add_comment` (or the tool can find it by branch/title)\n</next_steps>\n\n<checkpoint_title>Preview 3 release notes editorial update</checkpoint_title>",
